Article 52 "Adverse events following immunization (AEFI)" refers to adverse drug reactions caused by a qualified vaccine during or after standardized vaccination, which result in damage to the recipient's body tissues, organs, or functions, and for which none of the relevant parties is at fault.
The following circumstances are not considered adverse events following immunization:
(1) General reactions after vaccination caused by the inherent characteristics of the vaccine;
(2) Damage to the recipient caused by quality problems of the vaccine;
(3) Damage to the recipient caused by the vaccination unit's violation of the vaccination work standards, immunization procedures, vaccine use guidelines, or vaccination protocols;
(4) The recipient is in the incubation period or prodromal stage of a certain disease at the time of vaccination and coincidentally develops the disease after vaccination;
(5) The recipient has a contraindication specified in the vaccine package insert, and the recipient or the recipient's guardian fails to truthfully provide information on the recipient's health status and contraindications before vaccination, resulting in acute recurrence or exacerbation of the recipient's original disease after vaccination;
(6) Individual or group psychogenic reactions caused by psychological factors.

Article 81 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory department of the people's government at or above the provincial level shall confiscate the illegal income, the illegally produced or sold vaccine, and items such as raw materials, excipients, packaging materials, and equipment specifically used for the illegal production of the vaccine, order the suspension of production or business for rectification, and impose a fine of not less than fifteen times but not more than fifty times the value of the illegally produced or sold vaccine; if the value is less than 500,000 yuan, it shall be calculated as 500,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the relevant drug approval certificates shall be revoked, up to the drug manufacturing license, and the income earned from the unit during the period of the illegal act shall be confiscated from the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, key position personnel, and other responsible persons, and a fine of not less than 50% but not more than ten times the income earned shall be imposed, and they shall be prohibited from engaging in drug production and business activities for up to ten years or permanently, and the public security organ shall impose detention of not less than five days but not more than fifteen days:
(1) Providing false data, materials, samples, or engaging in other deceptive acts in applying for vaccine clinical trials, registration, or lot release;
(2) Fabricating production or inspection records or altering product batch numbers;
(3) A unit or individual other than a disease prevention and control institution supplying vaccines to a vaccination unit;
(4) Commissioning production of vaccines without approval;
(5) Changes in production process, production site, key equipment, or the like that are required to be approved in accordance with regulations but are made without approval;
(6) Updating the vaccine package insert or label without the approval required in accordance with regulations.

Article 83 In violation of the provisions of this Law, if a vaccine marketing authorization holder has any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory department of the people's government at or above the provincial level shall order rectification and give a warning; if the holder refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the holder shall be ordered to suspend production or business for rectification and shall be imposed a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan:
(1) Failing to establish a vaccine electronic traceability system in accordance with regulations;
(2) The legal representative, principal responsible person, production management responsible person, quality management responsible person, qualified person, or other key position personnel do not meet the required conditions, or the holder fails to train or assess them in accordance with regulations;
(3) Failing to report or file in accordance with regulations;
(4) Failing to conduct post-marketing studies in accordance with regulations, or failing to establish a unit or assign personnel to proactively collect, track, and analyze suspected adverse events following immunization in accordance with regulations;
(5) Failing to take out compulsory vaccine liability insurance in accordance with regulations;
(6) Failing to establish an information disclosure system in accordance with regulations.

Article 84 In violation of the provisions of this Law, if a lot release agency has any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory department of the State Council shall order rectification and give a warning, and the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given a warning up to demotion according to law:
(1) Failing to conduct review and testing in accordance with regulations;
(2) Failing to promptly publish the lot release results of marketed vaccines;
(3) Failing to verify in accordance with regulations;
(4) Discovering a significant quality risk in a vaccine and failing to report it in accordance with regulations.
In violation of the provisions of this Law, if a lot release agency fails to issue a lot release certificate or a notice of non-release in accordance with regulations, the drug regulatory department of the State Council shall order rectification and give a warning, and the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given demotion or removal from office according to law; if the circumstances are serious, the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given dismissal according to law.

Article 87 In violation of the provisions of this Law, if a disease prevention and control institution or vaccination unit has any of the following circumstances, the health department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification, give a warning, and confiscate the illegal income; if the circumstances are serious, the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given a warning up to removal from office according to law, and the responsible medical and health personnel shall be ordered to suspend their practice for not less than one year but not more than eighteen months; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given dismissal according to law, and the original issuing department shall revoke the practice certificate of the responsible medical and health personnel:
(1) Failing to supply, receive, or procure vaccines in accordance with regulations;
(2) Administering vaccines without complying with the vaccination work standards, immunization procedures, vaccine use guidelines, or vaccination protocols;
(3) Conducting mass vaccination without authorization.

Article 88 In violation of the provisions of this Law, if a disease prevention and control institution or vaccination unit has any of the following circumstances, the health department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification and give a warning; if the circumstances are serious, the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given a warning up to removal from office according to law, and the responsible medical and health personnel shall be ordered to suspend their practice for not less than six months but not more than one year; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor, and other directly responsible persons shall be given dismissal according to law, and the original issuing department shall revoke the practice certificate of the responsible medical and health personnel:
(1) Failing to provide traceability information in accordance with regulations;
(2) Failing to request and keep relevant certification documents and temperature monitoring records in accordance with regulations when receiving or purchasing vaccines;
(3) Failing to establish and keep records of vaccine receipt, purchase, storage, distribution, supply, administration, and disposal in accordance with regulations;
(4) Failing to inform or inquire about the relevant circumstances of the recipient or the recipient's guardian in accordance with regulations.

Article 94 If a local people's government at or above the county level has any of the following circumstances in vaccine supervision and management, the directly responsible supervisor and other directly responsible persons shall be given demotion or removal from office according to law; if the circumstances are serious, they shall be given dismissal according to law; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person shall resign to assume responsibility:
(1) Failing to perform duties effectively, causing serious adverse impact or significant losses;
(2) Concealing, making false reports, delaying reporting, or omitting reporting of vaccine safety incidents;
(3) Interfering with or obstructing the investigation of vaccine-related illegal acts or vaccine safety incidents;
(4) A particularly major vaccine safety incident occurs in the administrative region, or major vaccine safety incidents occur consecutively.

Article 95 If the drug regulatory department, health department, or other departments have any of the following circumstances in vaccine supervision and management, the directly responsible supervisor and other directly responsible persons shall be given demotion or removal from office according to law; if the circumstances are serious, they shall be given dismissal according to law; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person shall resign to assume responsibility:
(1) Failing to perform supervision and inspection duties, or failing to investigate and deal with illegal acts in a timely manner upon discovery;
(2) Conducting mass vaccination without authorization;
(3) Concealing, making false reports, delaying reporting, or omitting reporting of vaccine safety incidents;
(4) Interfering with or obstructing the investigation of vaccine-related illegal acts or vaccine safety incidents;
(5) Disclosing the information of a whistleblower;
(6) Upon receiving a report related to a suspected adverse event following immunization, failing to organize investigation and handling in accordance with regulations;
(7) Other failures to perform vaccine supervision and management duties, causing serious adverse impact or significant losses.
